    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d810">

                <pb facs="1095" n="1085" sameAs="frus:frus1945v07/pg1085"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.51/5–945</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chinese Minister for Foreign Affairs</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Soong</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Assistant Secretary of State</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Clayton</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-05-09">May 9, 1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Will</hi>: Enclosed please find copy of my
                    letter to Secretary Morgenthau. I am anxious to get his confirmation before I
                    leave for San Francisco,<anchor n="57" xml:id="d810-f1"/> as I understand he is
                    leaving for Florida tomorrow afternoon and will not be returning till next
                    Tuesday.</p>
                <p>In case I get his reply tomorrow I could return to San Francisco immediately; if
                    not, I will be bogged down till next week; in which case I hope Ed<anchor n="58"
                        xml:id="d810-f2"/> will understand I am not a willing delinquent.</p>
                <p>Thank you for your helpfulness in attending the conference this afternoon.</p>
                <p>Yours sincerely,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tse Vun Soong</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d810-a1.xml" xpointer="d810-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d810-f1" n="57" xml:id="d810-f1-content">
                <p>Dr. Soong was Chairman of the Chinese Delegation to the United Nations Conference
                    on International Organization at San Francisco.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d810-f2" n="58" xml:id="d810-f2-content">
                <p>Edward R. Stettinius, Jr., Chairman of the American Delegation.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
